course: dictionary
lesson: 2886
title: Words with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look ordinary but have a capital letter, which tells you they are a name. «Doric» with a capital D names a style, a people or a dialect. The context shows which one it is.
explain: Doric columns in art and history lessons are plain, thick and strong, with a simple round top. Ionic columns have scrolls and Corinthian columns have leaves. If the sentence is about columns or Ancient Greek buildings, Doric means the plain style.
explain: In Scotland, Doric is the name of the Scots dialect spoken in the north-east, around Aberdeen. A dialect is a local way of speaking a language. Some children there say «loon» for boy and «quine» for girl.
explain: «In the Doric dialect of north-east Scotland, "Fit like?" means how are you.» Here Doric is a dialect, and the sentence explains that "fit" is the local way of saying "what". Use the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Doric has three meanings: a plain style of ancient Greek column, a Scots dialect, and something to do with the Dorians, an ancient Greek people.
fact: «Doric» columns are thick and plain, with a simple round top, as on the Parthenon in Athens.
fact: «Doric» is the name of the Scots dialect spoken around Aberdeen in the north-east of Scotland.
fact: In Scotland, «loon» means boy and «quine» means girl.
fact: Doric is usually written with a capital D, because it is a name.
exercise: «The temple had thick, plain columns with simple round tops.» What style of column is this? | *Doric, plain and strong | Ionic, with scrolls | Gothic, with pointed arches | Corinthian, with leaves
exercise: Ayla hears a Doric word, «loon», while visiting Aberdeen. What does loon mean? | *A boy | A girl | A column | A Greek hero
exercise: Doric is the name of a dialect, so how should it be written at the start of a sentence? | *With a capital D | In capitals only when it is a question | With a small d | It should not be written at all
test: «The Parthenon in Athens has tall columns.» Which column style is plain, thick and strong? | Ionic | *Doric | Corinthian | Gothic
test: «The Dorians were one of the ancient Greek peoples.» What does Doric mean in a sentence about the Dorians? | *To do with the Dorians and their Greek dialect | Plain columns | A kind of cloud | Scots spoken in Aberdeen
exam: A Scottish friend asks, «Fit like?» What does it mean? | What time is it | Goodbye | Where are you | *How are you
